      en: "The Shore Temple at Mahabalipuram in Tamil Nadu is an 8th-century architectural masterpiece of the Pallava dynasty. It consists of three shrines dedicated to Shiva, built from granite blocks without mortar. The temple stands directly on the coast of the Bay of Bengal and has suffered damage from marine erosion and tsunamis. Its structure features pyramidal vimanas and elaborate relief carvings. The temple is part of the Group of Monuments at Mahabalipuram, designated a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1984. It served as a landmark for sailors and testifies to the maritime trade links of the Pallava Empire.",
