      en: "Jaisalmer Fort in Rajasthan is one of the largest fully preserved fortified cities in the world, often called the 'Golden Fort' due to its yellow sandstone construction. Built in 1156 CE by Rawal Jaisal, it sits on a hill in the Thar Desert. About a quarter of the city's population still resides within its walls, amid palaces, temples, and residential buildings. The architecture showcases Rajput style with intricate carvings. Four gates lead into the fort, protected by a 15 m (49 ft) thick wall. Jaisalmer Fort was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2013 as part of the Hill Forts of Rajasthan.",
