      en: "Sarnath, near Varanasi, is one of the most important Buddhist pilgrimage sites, as Buddha delivered his first sermon here after enlightenment, setting in motion the Wheel of Dharma. The archaeological site includes the Dhamek Stupa from the 5th century, 43.6 m (143 ft) high, along with ruins of monasteries and pillars. Notable is the Ashoka Pillar with its lion capital, which became India's national emblem. Sarnath flourished from the 3rd century BCE to the 12th century CE as a center of Buddhist learning. The nearby Mulagandha Kuti Vihar temple houses murals. Excavations have revealed sculptures and inscriptions.",
