      en: "Bibi Ka Maqbara, located in Aurangabad, Maharashtra, is a mausoleum built by Prince Azam Shah for his mother Dilras Banu Begum, wife of Emperor Aurangzeb. Completed between 1678 and 1679, it is often called the 'Mini Taj' due to its resemblance to the Taj Mahal, though it is smaller and less ornate. The structure is made of white marble and stands in a charbagh garden. It rises to a height of 58 meters, with a domed chamber and four minarets. The interior is decorated with intricate carvings and plasterwork. The tomb reflects the decline of Mughal patronage as it lacks the fine inlay work of earlier monuments.",
